LINUX COMMANDS USED IN THE PROJECT
==================================

1. pwd
-------
Displays the current working directory.

Command:
pwd


2. ls
------
Lists files and directories.

Command:
ls


3. cd
------
Changes the current directory.

Command:
cd project


4. mkdir
---------
Creates a new directory.

Command:
mkdir project


5. touch
---------
Creates a new empty file.

Command:
touch test.txt


6. cat
-------
Displays the contents of a file.

Command:
cat test.txt


7. cp
------
Copies files or directories.

Example:
cp test.txt backup.txt


8. mv
------
Moves or renames files.

Example:
mv test.txt newtest.txt


9. rm
------
Removes a file.

Example:
rm test.txt


10. chmod
---------
Changes file permissions.

Example:
chmod 755 demo.txt


11. ls -l
---------
Displays files with detailed information including permissions.

Command:
ls -l


12. useradd
-----------
Creates a new Linux user.

Example:
sudo useradd devuser


13. groupadd
------------
Creates a new group.

Example:
sudo groupadd developers


14. usermod
-----------
Adds a user to a group.

Example:
sudo usermod -aG developers devuser


15. groups
----------
Displays the groups associated with a user.

Example:
groups devuser


16. ps
------
Displays running processes.

Command:
ps


17. top
-------
Displays running processes and system resource usage.

Command:
top


18. kill
--------
Terminates a process.

Example:
kill <PID>


19. systemctl
------------
Manages Linux services.

Check Nginx status:
sudo systemctl status nginx

Start Nginx:
sudo systemctl start nginx

Stop Nginx:
sudo systemctl stop nginx

Restart Nginx:
sudo systemctl restart nginx

Enable Nginx at system startup:
sudo systemctl enable nginx


20. ip addr
-----------
Displays network interface and IP address information.

Command:
ip addr


21. hostname
------------
Displays the hostname of the server.

Command:
hostname


22. ping
--------
Tests network connectivity.

Example:
ping -c 4 google.com


23. curl
--------
Tests HTTP connectivity and retrieves content.

Example:
curl http://localhost


24. nginx -v
-----------
Displays the installed Nginx version.

Command:
nginx -v
